{{Quote|Saleucami has fallen, and Master Vos moved his troops to Boz Pity.|[[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]|<ref name="Revenge of the Sith">{{Film|III}}</ref>}}
'''Boz Pity''' was a [[planet]]<ref name="Collapse" /> located in the [[Boz Pity system]]<ref name="Star Wars 8" /> of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]],<ref name="TFABG" /> [[Kashyyyk Region]],<ref name="Route" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="Slice" /> During the [[High Republic Era]], it was considered a key member of the [[Galactic Republic]], and received a [[World Pavilions|sky-island]] with a representation of its environment at the [[Valo Republic Fair]].<ref name="Rising Storm" /> At some point prior to joining the [[mercenary]] outfit [[Zero Company]], the [[Mandalorian]] [[Clytemnestra Kullervo]] [[Death|killed]] eighteen [[Gamorrean]] [[enslaver]]s on Boz Pity.<ref name="ZeroCompany">''[[Star Wars Zero Company]]''</ref>

By the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]], Boz Pity was largely uninhabited, and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] established a presence on it during the conflict, enabling them to frequently strike at nearby [[Galactic Republic]] targets.<ref name="Collapse" /> The planet became one of the Confederacy's [[factory world]]s known as the [[Foundry of the Confederacy]] together with [[Metalorn]], [[Saleucami]], and [[Felucia]].<ref name="Battles" /> The [[Techno Union]] operated on Boz Pity in association with the factories.<ref name="OSWM 122" /> In response to the raids, Boz Pity became subject to a [[Siege of Boz Pity|siege]] by [[Republic Military|Republic forces]]<ref name="Collapse" /> of the [[12th Sector Army]] as part of the [[Outer Rim Sieges]].<ref name="Battles" /> The Siege of Boz Pity became one of the most intense battles of the Clone War and drew in major military members from both sides.<ref name="Collapse" /> Among them were the Separatist [[ST-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid]] [[Linwodo]] who had also defended Metalorn,<ref name="Battles" /> and [[Jedi General]] [[Quinlan Vos]] who moved his troops to support Boz Pity after the conclusion of the [[Siege of Saleucami]].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> Shortly after, both Linwodo and Vos were reassigned to the [[Battle of Kashyyyk]] which fought for the position at the doorstep of the Foundry.<ref name="Battles" /> Boz Pity was mentioned as a notable factory world by [[Muzzle]] in the survival compendium "[[Neyo's Almanac of Clankers]]."<ref name="OSWM 122" />

During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], the ''[[Ghost]]'', a [[light freighter]] used by the [[Spectres]], used a false [[transponder code]] that stated the [[freighter]] had free passage rights between [[Lothal]] and Boz Pity.<ref name="Idiot's Array">{{Rebels|Idiot's Array (episode)}}</ref> A [[Battle of Boz Pity (Galactic Civil War)|Battle of Boz Pity]], in which [[Gial Ackbar]] was injured, was fought during the Imperial Era.<ref name="Rebel Alliance Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Rebel Alliance}}</ref> At some point, [[Nath Tensent]], [[pilot]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] and later the [[New Republic]], was involved in a mission on Boz Pity and watched some of his friends [[Death|die]].<ref name="Alphabet Squadron">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Boz Pity was first mentioned in the current [[canon]] in the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> [[Boz Pity/Legends|Boz Pity]] was originally featured earlier that year in [[Obsession 4|the fourth issue]], the fourth issue of the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] series ''[[Star Wars: Obsession]]'', written by [[W. Haden Blackman]].<ref name="O4">[[Obsession 4|''Obsession'' 4]]</ref>

Boz Pity was originally meant to appear in the earliest iteration of the crash scene of the [[DTE-CSA-17 Calaboose prison ship|Republic prison transport]] ''[[Palwick]]'' transporting [[Verosha Aniseya|Osha Aniseya]] in the [[Lost / Found|first episode]] of the [[2024]] live-action TV series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', where it would have been a [[desert]] planet<ref name="Lost/Found-EG">{{SW|url=series/the-acolyte/lost-found-episode-guide|text="Lost / Found" Episode Guide &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref> as series creator [[Leslye Headland]] felt that it was "very ''[[Star Wars]]''". In the original scene, Aniseya would have wandered across the desert and concept art of the area was created by [[Adam Brockbank]], [[Doug Chiang]] and [[Jama Jurabaev]] and showed a dusty environment with enormous stone pillars and giant animal [[skeleton]]s. However, production designer [[Kevin Jenkins]] said that, although he though that the idea was cool, that they couldn't do another desert for financial reasons.<ref name="ArtofAcolyte">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''</ref> The filmmakers then later instead pivoted to a cold planet and chose Carlac which had previously first appeared in the [[The Clone Wars: Season Four|''The Clone Wars'' Season Four]]<ref name="Lost/Found-EG" /> episode "[[A Friend in Need]]".<ref name="A Friend in Need">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref>

